  French translation of values/strings_backup.xml — the backup and restore copy.
  The comments below are the source file's translator notes, kept in English on
  purpose: they explain why a string is worded the way it is, and they are notes
  to maintainers rather than UI text.
-->
<resources>
    <string name="job_backing_up">Sauvegarde en cours</string>
    <string name="job_restoring">Restauration en cours</string>
    <!--
      Here rather than in values/strings.xml with the rest of the export copy, because this is a job
      *title* and titleFor() reads all three from one place. It also inherits this file's
      MissingTranslation exemption, which its two siblings already rely on; the export sentences it
      appears above are translated, since they live in the enforced file.
    -->
    <string name="job_exporting">Exportation en cours</string>
    <!--
      Named for the channel's scope, not for the feature that opened it. A user silencing this is
      silencing every long-running job Thor reports — bulk actions are meant to join backups on it —
      and a switch labelled "Backup and restore" would not have told them that. The channel id is
      unchanged ("thor.jobs"), so renaming it here renames the existing switch rather than creating a
      second one; a channel's name is updatable, its importance is not once the user has touched it.
    -->
    <string name="job_channel_name">Tâches en arrière-plan</string>
    <string name="job_channel_description">Progression des exportations, sauvegardes, restaurations et actions groupées en cours en arrière-plan</string>

